WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:01.245
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.245 --> 00:00:02.671
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.671 --> 00:00:03.997
My one word is believe.

00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:06.069
I believe that entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:08.182
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:10.057
To help you on your
journey, today's message

00:00:10.057 --> 00:00:13.639
is turn your weaknesses
into your strengths.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:15.984
Over to you John Jocko Willink.

00:00:15.984 --> 00:00:18.085
(rooster crows)

00:00:18.085 --> 00:00:20.637
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:23.420
♫ Espresso get me going.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.436
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.436 --> 00:00:31.603
- A person's strengths are
often their biggest weaknesses.

00:00:32.586 --> 00:00:35.669
That also means that their weaknesses

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.007
can be their strengths.

00:00:43.156 --> 00:00:43.989
Me?

00:00:45.641 --> 00:00:46.474
I am weak.

00:00:47.637 --> 00:00:50.004
In all those ways that I listed.

00:00:50.004 --> 00:00:50.837
I am weak.

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:56.676
But I don't accept that.

00:00:56.676 --> 00:00:59.271
I don't accept that I am what I am

00:00:59.271 --> 00:01:02.521
and that that is what I'm doomed to be.

00:01:04.873 --> 00:01:07.460
No, I don't accept that.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.543
I'm fighting.

00:01:09.771 --> 00:01:11.019
I always fighting.

00:01:11.019 --> 00:01:14.266
I'm struggling and I'm scrapping

00:01:14.266 --> 00:01:17.754
and I'm kicking and
clawing at those weaknesses

00:01:17.754 --> 00:01:20.171
to change them, to stop them.

00:01:23.372 --> 00:01:24.705
Some days I win.

00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:29.104
Some days I don't.

00:01:30.517 --> 00:01:34.020
But each and every day, I get back up,

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.520
and I move forward

00:01:37.381 --> 00:01:40.829
with my fists clenched toward the battle,

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:42.496
toward the struggle.

00:01:44.272 --> 00:01:46.477
And I fight with everything I've got

00:01:46.477 --> 00:01:49.384
to overcome those weaknesses
and those shortfalls

00:01:49.384 --> 00:01:50.717
and those flaws.

00:01:52.358 --> 00:01:56.358
As I strive to be just a
little bit better today

00:01:59.154 --> 00:02:01.007
than I was yesterday.

00:02:01.007 --> 00:02:02.319
- I don't really spend
a lot of time thinking

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:03.664
about my weaknesses.

00:02:03.664 --> 00:02:05.616
I think it's important
to have the awareness

00:02:05.616 --> 00:02:07.601
to know what you're not good at,

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:09.729
to know that you might suck at accounting

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.297
or you might suck at sales and marketing

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.138
or you might not be great
in front of the camera

00:02:13.138 --> 00:02:15.224
or you might not want to write copy,

00:02:15.224 --> 00:02:16.530
like, you're not good at these things.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.273
It's good to know what you're good at

00:02:19.273 --> 00:02:21.179
and know what you're great at.

00:02:21.179 --> 00:02:22.492
So you can focus your time.

00:02:22.492 --> 00:02:23.524
This is your goal, right?

00:02:23.524 --> 00:02:25.475
You're goal is to focus
as much time on the things

00:02:25.475 --> 00:02:28.587
that you can potentially be
one of the greatest people

00:02:28.587 --> 00:02:30.067
in the world at.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:34.159
I'm not a big fan of focusing
on improving your weaknesses.

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:38.322
I think you have people who
you're great at this one thing.

00:02:38.322 --> 00:02:40.236
You could be up here shining like a star.

00:02:40.236 --> 00:02:43.724
You've got Michael Jordan
genius-level talent at this

00:02:43.724 --> 00:02:46.347
and you suck at all these other things.

00:02:46.347 --> 00:02:49.070
And you either focus your
time trying to improve

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.645
all these things that you're not good at

00:02:51.645 --> 00:02:53.627
and spend time and
improve and work on them

00:02:53.627 --> 00:02:57.859
and slowly get better and
maybe get average results.

00:02:57.859 --> 00:03:00.907
Or you can ignore all this
stuff and focus on this

00:03:00.907 --> 00:03:03.263
and be amazing at it.

00:03:03.263 --> 00:03:04.854
I want to be up here.

00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:06.712
I don't want to focus down here.

00:03:06.712 --> 00:03:09.800
The world rewards the
people who play up here.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.178
The world rewards the people
who are amazing at something,

00:03:13.178 --> 00:03:16.046
can provide insane value at something.

00:03:16.046 --> 00:03:18.728
You get success by
providing value to people.

00:03:18.728 --> 00:03:21.691
If you are average at a
whole bunch of things,

00:03:21.691 --> 00:03:23.354
you're not really
providing a lot of value.

00:03:23.354 --> 00:03:25.687
But if you're great at this one thing.

00:03:25.687 --> 00:03:28.072
If you are the world's greatest mechanic,

00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:30.423
you can provide a ton of value to people.

00:03:30.423 --> 00:03:31.856
You can make a ton of money.

00:03:31.856 --> 00:03:33.239
You can have a huge impact

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:36.090
'cause you are the
world's greatest mechanic

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.008
or surgeon, or basketball
player, or coder,

00:03:39.008 --> 00:03:42.080
or videographer, or whatever
it is that you can be great at.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.936
And who cares if you can't sing

00:03:44.936 --> 00:03:46.312
or if you suck at math

00:03:46.312 --> 00:03:47.712
or if you don't know you're accounting

00:03:47.712 --> 00:03:50.107
or if your spelling is off.

00:03:50.107 --> 00:03:52.048
For me, this stuff doesn't matter.

00:03:52.048 --> 00:03:53.353
Focus up on here.

00:03:53.353 --> 00:03:57.216
I think, too much, we
talk about trying to work

00:03:57.216 --> 00:04:00.430
on our weaknesses and trying
to improve these sayings.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.477
It's a noble effort but the biggest factor

00:04:03.477 --> 00:04:05.034
is its opportunity cost.

00:04:05.034 --> 00:04:06.779
You're taking away from doing this thing

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:07.994
that you're great at.

00:04:07.994 --> 00:04:10.038
You're taking away from
spending your time up here

00:04:10.038 --> 00:04:12.331
being a star, working your craft,

00:04:12.331 --> 00:04:15.924
because having a natural
talent isn't enough.

00:04:15.924 --> 00:04:17.204
You could be the world's
greatest mechanic,

00:04:17.204 --> 00:04:18.883
but, you need to practice.

00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:20.202
Michael Jordan might
be the world's greatest

00:04:20.202 --> 00:04:21.755
basketball player, but he practiced.

00:04:21.755 --> 00:04:23.296
Every day, he practiced.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.019
He practiced, he practiced, he practiced.

00:04:25.019 --> 00:04:27.418
He was the first one to come
in and the last one to leave

00:04:27.418 --> 00:04:28.561
and all the cliches.

00:04:28.561 --> 00:04:30.465
He worked hard.

00:04:30.465 --> 00:04:33.186
And that time, we all
have 24 hours of the day,

00:04:33.186 --> 00:04:36.607
that time, if he was spending
it doing non-basketball stuff

00:04:36.607 --> 00:04:40.717
that he didn't care about,
he wouldn't have the leverage

00:04:40.717 --> 00:04:43.672
even though he might have
natural talent for basketball.

00:04:43.672 --> 00:04:45.672
Because he wasn't working it hard,

00:04:45.672 --> 00:04:47.126
he wasn't going to have success.

00:04:47.126 --> 00:04:49.760
So, I think you need to
have the self-awareness

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.034
to understand what your weaknesses are.

00:04:53.034 --> 00:04:55.392
The best entrepreneurs in
the world understand that.

00:04:55.392 --> 00:04:56.768
They know what they're great at

00:04:56.768 --> 00:04:59.361
and they know what they
absolutely suck at.

00:04:59.361 --> 00:05:01.057
And what they're great at is usually one

00:05:01.057 --> 00:05:02.612
or two or three things, that's it.

00:05:02.612 --> 00:05:04.598
Like, a really tiny handful of things,

00:05:04.598 --> 00:05:06.452
that's what they're great at.

00:05:06.452 --> 00:05:09.163
And then they build up
a team to support them

00:05:09.163 --> 00:05:10.899
in all the areas that they're weak at.

00:05:10.899 --> 00:05:13.139
So, I can spend my time
doing what I love to do,

00:05:13.139 --> 00:05:15.084
what I could be world's
best at potentially,

00:05:15.084 --> 00:05:16.133
and I'm working towards.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:17.759
I look at this YouTube channel.

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:19.954
When I started it, it was all me.

00:05:19.954 --> 00:05:21.133
And you have to have that approach

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:22.700
that you're going to
do everything yourself.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.174
I will be an army of one.

00:05:24.174 --> 00:05:25.392
I will try to enlist help,

00:05:25.392 --> 00:05:27.373
get people to volunteer their time,

00:05:27.373 --> 00:05:29.263
try to get people on
board with what I'm doing.

00:05:29.263 --> 00:05:30.595
But if I can't at the start,

00:05:30.595 --> 00:05:32.893
'cause I don't want to spend
money 'til I'm making money,

00:05:32.893 --> 00:05:34.013
I'll be an army of one.

00:05:34.013 --> 00:05:35.951
I will will it into existence.

00:05:35.951 --> 00:05:36.980
I will just create it.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:37.813
I will do everything.

00:05:37.813 --> 00:05:38.989
I will film it, I will edit it,

00:05:38.989 --> 00:05:40.445
I'll be in front of the
camera, behind the camera,

00:05:40.445 --> 00:05:42.534
researching, publishing, everything.

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:45.821
But I realize that my strength

00:05:45.821 --> 00:05:47.590
and what I want to get better at,

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:52.375
is going to be the stuff in
front of the camera, not behind.

00:05:52.375 --> 00:05:53.495
I don't really want to learn

00:05:53.495 --> 00:05:54.823
how to be a better videographer.

00:05:54.823 --> 00:05:57.888
I don't really want to learn
how to position the lights

00:05:57.888 --> 00:05:59.630
and be the best lighting guy in the world.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.710
I don't really want to learn
about different microphones

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.743
and the technology and all of
the stuff dealing with sound.

00:06:04.743 --> 00:06:07.312
I don't really want to learn
about a lot of the stuff

00:06:07.312 --> 00:06:09.645
that has to do with my YouTube channel.

00:06:09.645 --> 00:06:10.967
I want to be in front of the camera

00:06:10.967 --> 00:06:12.448
and be as good as I can be

00:06:12.448 --> 00:06:14.039
and practice and work hard

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:17.505
and make thousands of videos,
5,000 videos I've made,

00:06:17.505 --> 00:06:20.802
to improve, to get better,
to work on my craft.

00:06:20.802 --> 00:06:22.606
And I want to improve
every video that goes out.

00:06:22.606 --> 00:06:25.150
I want to make sure that
it passes my quality test.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.028
I see every video that we
have before it launches

00:06:28.028 --> 00:06:30.090
and I say, "Yes, I'm proud of this.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.652
"I will show my grandkids this.

00:06:31.652 --> 00:06:33.932
"This passes the Evan Carmichael test."

00:06:33.932 --> 00:06:36.004
I want to keep raising the bar on that.

00:06:36.004 --> 00:06:38.972
For me to focus my time
on making more videos

00:06:38.972 --> 00:06:41.710
that practice my skill,
and to review the videos

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.684
that are coming in, the amount
of time that that takes,

00:06:43.684 --> 00:06:46.333
I can't be spending it on other stuff.

00:06:46.333 --> 00:06:48.229
When I was doing everything all myself,

00:06:48.229 --> 00:06:50.790
I was lucky to make one video a month

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.868
and eventually move to one video a week,

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:56.172
maximum 'cause I was doing everything.

00:06:56.172 --> 00:06:58.412
As I hired my first
person who was an editor,

00:06:58.412 --> 00:07:01.820
I could move from a video
to a week to a video a day.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.636
And as I started building up more team,

00:07:03.636 --> 00:07:07.271
as I made more money, then
I could hire more people

00:07:07.271 --> 00:07:08.914
and I could make more videos to two a day

00:07:08.914 --> 00:07:10.416
to now three a day.

00:07:10.416 --> 00:07:11.249
So, think about it.

00:07:11.249 --> 00:07:13.418
Three video a day versus one video a week.

00:07:13.418 --> 00:07:15.717
How much better am I going to
get in front of the camera?

00:07:15.717 --> 00:07:17.287
I hope a little bit better, right?

00:07:17.287 --> 00:07:20.411
How many more videos am
I going to have to review

00:07:20.411 --> 00:07:22.158
to keep raising the bar on the quality

00:07:22.158 --> 00:07:25.157
and hone my eye on what I
think makes a good video.

00:07:25.157 --> 00:07:27.365
I'm getting the repetitions
in so my muscle gets strong

00:07:27.365 --> 00:07:30.442
and I get better at the thing
that I want to get better at.

00:07:30.442 --> 00:07:32.245
If you're not spending any of your time,

00:07:32.245 --> 00:07:35.062
if you're spending 80% of
your time, 95% of your time,

00:07:35.062 --> 00:07:36.380
working on the things that you suck at

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:38.904
just to try to get to mediocre level,

00:07:38.904 --> 00:07:40.531
and only five to 20% of your time

00:07:40.531 --> 00:07:43.212
with things that you have
a chance to be a star at,

00:07:43.212 --> 00:07:44.331
you're never going to reach it.

00:07:44.331 --> 00:07:45.563
You're never going to get there.

00:07:45.563 --> 00:07:47.652
You're going to be average at best.

00:07:47.652 --> 00:07:52.135
I want you to have an allergic
reaction to being average.

00:07:52.135 --> 00:07:53.611
I want you to find the thing that you

00:07:53.611 --> 00:07:56.075
have the amazing ability to shine at,

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:59.538
to be Michael Jordan-level
talent, genius-level talent at,

00:07:59.538 --> 00:08:02.603
and try to spend as much
time doing that as possible.

00:08:02.603 --> 00:08:05.075
Put in the reps so you could feel

00:08:05.075 --> 00:08:07.096
like you're having a big impact.

00:08:07.096 --> 00:08:08.907
So you can feel like you're growing,

00:08:08.907 --> 00:08:10.213
you're making a lot of money,

00:08:10.213 --> 00:08:12.803
you're doing a lot of
damage in your industry

00:08:12.803 --> 00:08:14.115
and you fulfill it.

00:08:14.115 --> 00:08:15.705
So, the question of the
day today is two part.

00:08:15.705 --> 00:08:18.033
I want to know what your
greatest strength is

00:08:18.033 --> 00:08:20.419
and what your greatest
weakness is as well.

00:08:20.419 --> 00:08:21.618
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:08:21.618 --> 00:08:22.784
I'm super curious about that.

00:08:22.784 --> 00:08:25.210
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Gavin Anderson.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.113
Gavin, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:08:27.113 --> 00:08:28.920
of my book, Your One Word.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.514
I really appreciate your support

00:08:30.514 --> 00:08:32.374
and I hope you enjoyed the book.

00:08:32.374 --> 00:08:34.006
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:08:34.006 --> 00:08:35.103
I believe in you.

00:08:35.103 --> 00:08:36.984
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:08:36.984 --> 00:08:39.311
and whatever your one word is.

00:08:39.311 --> 00:08:41.622
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:08:41.622 --> 00:08:44.838
for another shot of entspresso.

00:08:44.838 --> 00:08:47.320
♫ I wake up every morning

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.653
♫ Espresso get me going

00:08:54.094 --> 00:08:57.144
- Knowing your strength and weaknesses

00:08:57.144 --> 00:09:00.431
and knowing what you enjoy doing.

00:09:00.431 --> 00:09:03.542
If you look at it as a
job, you've already lost.

00:09:03.542 --> 00:09:05.301
It's not going to be your passion

00:09:05.301 --> 00:09:07.199
and you're going to count the hours.

00:09:07.199 --> 00:09:10.949
If you look at it as
something you love to do

00:09:12.697 --> 00:09:14.781
and then you know what your strengths are,

00:09:14.781 --> 00:09:18.142
then you can leverage those
strengths in your business

00:09:18.142 --> 00:09:19.663
and in helping others.

00:09:19.663 --> 00:09:21.647
Once you recognize your weaknesses,

00:09:21.647 --> 00:09:24.761
then you can work with
people that complement you.

00:09:24.761 --> 00:09:26.215
Every one of my businesses,

00:09:26.215 --> 00:09:29.215
I've had a partner who is very anal.

00:09:30.187 --> 00:09:32.370
Martin Woodall, Todd Wagner.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:35.266
I mean, incredibly anal
people, perfectionists,

00:09:35.266 --> 00:09:36.894
'cause I'm a slob.

00:09:36.894 --> 00:09:39.783
I'm a big picture, think about
what's around the corner,

00:09:39.783 --> 00:09:41.527
how's technology going to change things?

00:09:41.527 --> 00:09:44.110
How can I change this industry?

00:09:45.248 --> 00:09:47.330
Making sure that there's
somebody there to dot the i's,

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:50.913
cross the t's and keep
me in the baselines.

00:09:52.486 --> 00:09:55.323
Recognizing my weaknesses
is just as important

00:09:55.323 --> 00:09:58.205
as recognizing my strengths,
my core competencies,

00:09:58.205 --> 00:10:00.788
and having a passion to do 'em.

00:10:01.813 --> 00:10:04.252
- Being intuitive is important.

00:10:04.252 --> 00:10:08.543
Surround yourself with
really smart business people

00:10:08.543 --> 00:10:11.090
that can support your weaknesses.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.822
Know what they are.

00:10:12.822 --> 00:10:15.920
I know I don't know how to
create an e-commerce platform.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.167
I'm well aware of that.

00:10:18.167 --> 00:10:21.390
So, I surrounded myself
with people who can

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.973
and who do do that.

00:10:24.797 --> 00:10:28.233
As far as mentors go, countless.

00:10:28.233 --> 00:10:32.400
I was not shy about making
phone calls to many people.

00:10:33.261 --> 00:10:37.801
I've been fortunate enough to
know people like Tori Merch

00:10:37.801 --> 00:10:40.146
and Diane Von Furstenburg.

00:10:40.146 --> 00:10:44.395
They got lots of emails
and phone calls from me

00:10:44.395 --> 00:10:47.308
along the way with
tears in my eyes saying,

00:10:47.308 --> 00:10:48.987
"I don't know if this is possible.

00:10:48.987 --> 00:10:51.025
"Why is everyone telling me, 'No'?

00:10:51.025 --> 00:10:52.353
"What do I do?

00:10:52.353 --> 00:10:55.666
"What does it even mean to
go to get venture capital?

00:10:55.666 --> 00:10:57.251
"What is venture capital?

00:10:57.251 --> 00:10:58.273
"What's a board?"

00:10:58.273 --> 00:11:01.491
I just didn't know all
these business terms.

00:11:01.491 --> 00:11:03.882
They helped me understand it.

00:11:03.882 --> 00:11:07.667
- It's very important, and
I also come back to chess,

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:11.270
to learn how to recognize your
own strengths and weaknesses.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.372
This is, in fact, the
vital part of preparation

00:11:14.372 --> 00:11:17.836
for a big match and for anything in life.

00:11:17.836 --> 00:11:20.015
We always try to study our opponents.

00:11:20.015 --> 00:11:22.592
We always try to study the battlefield.

00:11:22.592 --> 00:11:25.098
We always try to study
all the circumstances

00:11:25.098 --> 00:11:27.799
surrounding our venture or endeavor.

00:11:27.799 --> 00:11:31.501
But, very often, we
forget to study ourself.

00:11:31.501 --> 00:11:34.084
And this is very important
because any choice

00:11:34.084 --> 00:11:36.350
of a ground for battle

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:39.933
or, you know, type of
strategy you want to employ,

00:11:39.933 --> 00:11:42.201
depends on our recognition

00:11:42.201 --> 00:11:45.131
of our strengths and weaknesses.

00:11:45.131 --> 00:11:47.748
And this is process of
constant re-evaluation

00:11:47.748 --> 00:11:50.098
because life is changing very fast.

00:11:50.098 --> 00:11:52.777
Our opponents, looking at our success,

00:11:52.777 --> 00:11:55.306
studying it and trying to be smart

00:11:55.306 --> 00:11:57.556
and outsmart us eventually.

00:11:58.529 --> 00:12:01.368
We can look at the history just to find

00:12:01.368 --> 00:12:03.701
a number of situations where

00:12:05.456 --> 00:12:08.448
the inability to recognize
strengths and weaknesses

00:12:08.448 --> 00:12:10.774
led to an eventual disaster.

